The excerpts say the models are evaluated using perplexity for language-model performance, and for bias evaluation they use “an array of metrics” including:

- co-occurrence bias, computed from model-generated texts by comparing occurrences of gender-neutral words with female and male words;
- conditional co-occurrence bias, a normalized version of co-occurrence bias;
- causal occupation bias, measured from paired/template samples where gender information differs;
- embedding bias, defined using gender-neutral occupations as the difference between Euclidean distances of an occupation word to male words and to female counterparts, equivalent to bias by projection.

The excerpts also mention occupation biases and gender-pair-based metrics, but the specific metric names/formulas are replaced by placeholders such as INLINEFORM0, INLINEFORM1, etc., so they cannot be recovered exactly from the provided text.

Answer: perplexity, co-occurrence bias, conditional co-occurrence bias, causal occupation bias, and embedding bias
